            <div xml:id="d952">

                <pb facs="1224" n="1214" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.9331/11–1946: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-22T19:00:00-05:00">November 22,
                            1946—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2131. Your recent message re Sinkiang (2271, Nov 19) not clear Dept, particularly
                    phrase “rejected and preempted by him in that he has already offered concessions
                    to Soviets that do involve political sovereignty”. Who has offered concessions
                    and do you know what they are?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
